{"id":"mahabharata-2-042","work":"mahabharata","part":2,"partName":"सभापर्व","partNameEn":"Sabha Parva","unit":42,"title":"द्विचत्वारिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 42 · The death of Shishupala; the sacrifice completed","summary":{"en":"Krishna recounts Shishupala's crimes against the Yadavas and declares his hundred pardons spent; he hurls his discus and cuts off Shishupala's head, and a radiance rises from the body and enters Krishna. Yudhishthira completes the Rajasuya and crowns Shishupala's son; the kings depart, but Duryodhana and Shakuni stay on in the hall.","kn":"ಯಾದವರ ವಿರುದ್ಧ ಶಿಶುಪಾಲನ ಅಪರಾಧಗಳನ್ನು ಹೇಳಿ ನೂರು ಕ್ಷಮೆಗಳು ಮುಗಿದವು ಎಂದು ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣನು ಘೋಷಿಸಿ ಚಕ್ರದಿಂದ ಅವನ ತಲೆ ಕತ್ತರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ದೇಹದಿಂದ ಒಂದು ತೇಜಸ್ಸು ಎದ್ದು ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣನಲ್ಲಿ ಸೇರುತ್ತದೆ. ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ರಾಜಸೂಯ ಪೂರೈಸಿ ಶಿಶುಪಾಲನ ಮಗನಿಗೆ ಪಟ್ಟಕಟ್ಟುತ್ತಾನೆ; ರಾಜರು ಹೊರಡುತ್ತಾರೆ, ಆದರೆ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ ಶಕುನಿ ಸಭೆಯಲ್ಲೇ ಉಳಿಯುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"श्रीकृष्ण यादवों के विरुद्ध शिशुपाल के अपराध गिनाकर घोषणा करते हैं कि उसके सौ क्षमादान पूरे हो गए; वे चक्र चलाकर उसका सिर काट देते हैं, और शरीर से एक तेज निकलकर श्रीकृष्ण में समा जाता है। युधिष्ठिर राजसूय पूरा कर शिशुपाल के पुत्र का अभिषेक करते हैं; राजा विदा होते हैं, पर दुर्योधन और शकुनि सभा में ठहरे रहते हैं।","te":"యాదవులపై శిశుపాలుని అపరాధాలను వివరించి నూరు క్షమలు ముగిశాయని శ్రీకృష్ణుడు ప్రకటించి చక్రంతో అతని తల నరుకుతాడు; దేహం నుండి ఒక తేజస్సు లేచి శ్రీకృష్ణునిలో లీనమవుతుంది. యుధిష్ఠిరుడు రాజసూయం పూర్తి చేసి శిశుపాలుని కుమారునికి పట్టం కడతాడు; రాజులు వెళ్తారు, కానీ దుర్యోధనుడు, శకుని సభలోనే ఉండిపోతారు.","ta":"யாதவர்களுக்கு எதிரான ஶிஶுபாலனின் குற்றங்களைச் சொல்லி நூறு மன்னிப்புகளும் தீர்ந்தன என்று ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணர் அறிவித்துச் சக்கரத்தால் அவன் தலையைத் துண்டிக்க, உடலிலிருந்து ஓர் ஒளி எழுந்து ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணரில் கலக்கிறது. யுதிஷ்டிரர் ராஜஸூயத்தை நிறைவு செய்து ஶிஶுபாலனின் மகனுக்கு முடிசூட்டுகிறார்; மன்னர்கள் புறப்பட, துரியோதனனும் ஶகுனியும் ஸபையிலேயே தங்குகிறார்கள்.","ml":"കൃഷ്ണൻ ശിശുപാലന്റെ യാദവർക്കെതിരായ കുറ്റങ്ങൾ വിവരിക്കുന്നു; അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ നൂറു പൊറുതികൾ തീർന്നുവെന്ന് പ്രഖ്യാപിക്കുന്നു. ചക്രമെറിഞ്ഞ് അദ്ദേഹം ശിശുപാലന്റെ തല അറുക്കുന്നു; ശരീരത്തിൽനിന്ന് ഒരു പ്രകാശം ഉയർന്ന് കൃഷ്ണനിൽ ലയിക്കുന്നു. യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ രാജസൂയം പൂർത്തിയാക്കുന്നു, ശിശുപാലന്റെ പുത്രനെ കിരീടമണിയിക്കുന്നു; രാജാക്കന്മാർ മടങ്ങുന്നു, എന്നാൽ ദുര്യോധനനും ശകുനിയും സദസ്സിൽ തങ്ങുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 2.42; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Apr 19 2006","sections":[{"title":"शिशुपालवधपर्व","titleEn":"Shishupalavadha Parva (Slaying of Shishupala)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततः श्रुत्वैव भीष्मस्य चेदिराडुरुविक्रमः ।\nयुयुत्सुर्वासुदेवेन वासुदेवमुवाच ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, on hearing Bhishma, the mighty king of Chedi, eager to fight Vasudeva, said to him:"}},{"n":2,"text":"आह्वये त्वां रणं गच्छ मया सार्धं जनार्दन ।\nयावदद्य निहन्मि त्वां सहितं सर्वपाण्डवैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shishupala said: I challenge you, Janardana: come to battle with me, until I kill you today along with all the Pandavas."}},{"n":3,"text":"सह त्वया हि मे वध्याः पाण्डवाः कृष्ण सर्वथा ।\nनृपतीन्समतिक्रम्य यैरराजा त्वमर्चितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna, the Pandavas too deserve death with you in every way, for they honoured you, no king, above the kings."}},{"n":4,"text":"ये त्वां दासमराजानं बाल्यादर्चन्ति दुर्मतिम् ।\nअनर्हमर्हवत्कृष्ण वध्यास्त इति मे मतिः ।\nइत्युक्त्वा राजशार्दूलस्तस्थौ गर्जन्नमर्षणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who from folly honour you, a slave and no king, an evil-minded unworthy man, as though worthy: in my view, Krishna, they deserve death. So saying, that tiger among kings stood roaring, unforgiving."}},{"n":5,"text":"एवमुक्ते ततः कृष्णो मृदुपूर्वमिदं वचः ।\nउवाच पार्थिवान्सर्वांस्तत्समक्षं च पाण्डवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When he had spoken so, Krishna said these words, gently at first, to all the kings and, in their presence, to the Pandavas:"}},{"n":6,"text":"एष नः शत्रुरत्यन्तं पार्थिवाः सात्वतीसुतः ।\nसात्वतानां नृशंसात्मा न हितोऽनपकारिणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna said: Kings, this son of Satvati is utterly our enemy; cruel-hearted, he has done no good to the Satvatas who had not wronged him."}},{"n":7,"text":"प्राग्ज्योतिषपुरं यातानस्माञ्ज्ञात्वा नृशंसकृत् ।\nअदहद्द्वारकामेष स्वस्रीयः सन्नराधिपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing we had gone to Pragjyotisha, this doer of cruel acts burnt Dvaraka, though he was our sister's son, lords of men."}},{"n":8,"text":"क्रीडतो भोजराजन्यानेष रैवतके गिरौ ।\nहत्वा बद्ध्वा च तान्सर्वानुपायात्स्वपुरं पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Once, when the Bhoja princes were playing on Mount Raivataka, he killed and bound them all and took them to his city."}},{"n":9,"text":"अश्वमेधे हयं मेध्यमुत्सृष्टं रक्षिभिर्वृतम् ।\nपितुर्मे यज्ञविघ्नार्थमहरत्पापनिश्चयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At my father's horse sacrifice, this man of wicked purpose carried off the sacrificial horse, released and guarded, to obstruct the sacrifice."}},{"n":10,"text":"सौवीरान्प्रतिपत्तौ च बभ्रोरेष यशस्विनः ।\nभार्यामभ्यहरन्मोहादकामां तामितो गताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the land of the Sauviras, he also seized in his folly the wife of renowned Babhru, who was travelling there unwillingly."}},{"n":11,"text":"एष मायाप्रतिच्छन्नः करूषार्थे तपस्विनीम् ।\nजहार भद्रां वैशालीं मातुलस्य नृशंसकृत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hidden in illusion, this doer of cruelty also carried off Bhadra of Vishala, the ascetic maiden, my mother's brother's daughter, for the sake of the Karusha king."}},{"n":12,"text":"पितृष्वसुः कृते दुःखं सुमहन्मर्षयाम्यहम् ।\nदिष्ट्या त्विदं सर्वराज्ञां संनिधावद्य वर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"For the sake of my father's sister, I have borne great suffering; by good fortune this comes before all the kings today."}},{"n":13,"text":"पश्यन्ति हि भवन्तोऽद्य मय्यतीव व्यतिक्रमम् ।\nकृतानि तु परोक्षं मे यानि तानि निबोधत ॥","meaning":{"en":"You see how greatly he has offended against me today; but hear what he did out of my sight."}},{"n":14,"text":"इमं त्वस्य न शक्ष्यामि क्षन्तुमद्य व्यतिक्रमम् ।\nअवलेपाद्वधार्हस्य समग्रे राजमण्डले ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall not be able to forgive this offence of his today, in the whole circle of kings, for he deserves death for his arrogance."}},{"n":15,"text":"रुक्मिण्यामस्य मूढस्य प्रार्थनासीन्मुमूर्षतः ।\nन च तां प्राप्तवान्मूढः शूद्रो वेदश्रुतिं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"This fool, wishing to die, desired Rukmini, but the fool did not get her, as a Shudra does not get the hearing of the Veda."}},{"n":16,"text":"एवमादि ततः सर्वे सहितास्ते नराधिपाः ।\nवासुदेववचः श्रुत्वा चेदिराजं व्यगर्हयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing Vasudeva's words, all those kings together, and more such things, rebuked the king of Chedi."}},{"n":17,"text":"ततस्तद्वचनं श्रुत्वा शिशुपालः प्रतापवान् ।\nजहास स्वनवद्धासं प्रहस्येदमुवाच ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, hearing those words, mighty Shishupala laughed loudly, and having laughed, said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"मत्पूर्वां रुक्मिणीं कृष्ण संसत्सु परिकीर्तयन् ।\nविशेषतः पार्थिवेषु व्रीडां न कुरुषे कथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shishupala said: Krishna, how can you declare in assemblies, especially among kings, Rukmini as one who was first mine, without being ashamed?"}},{"n":19,"text":"मन्यमानो हि कः सत्सु पुरुषः परिकीर्तयेत् ।\nअन्यपूर्वां स्त्रियं जातु त्वदन्यो मधुसूदन ॥","meaning":{"en":"What man other than you, Madhusudana, in the presence of the good, would ever proclaim a woman who was first another's, while thinking of himself as respectable?"}},{"n":20,"text":"क्षम वा यदि ते श्रद्धा मा वा कृष्ण मम क्षम ।\nक्रुद्धाद्वापि प्रसन्नाद्वा किं मे त्वत्तो भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Forgive me, Krishna, if you have faith, or do not; whether angry or pleased, what will come to me from you?"}},{"n":21,"text":"तथा ब्रुवत एवास्य भगवान्मधुसूदनः ।\nव्यपाहरच्छिरः क्रुद्धश्चक्रेणामित्रकर्षणः ।\nस पपात महाबाहुर्वज्राहत इवाचलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he spoke thus, the blessed Madhusudana, destroyer of foes, angrily cut off his head with the discus; and that mighty-armed man fell like a mountain struck by thunder."}},{"n":22,"text":"ततश्चेदिपतेर्देहात्तेजोऽग्र्यं ददृशुर्नृपाः ।\nउत्पतन्तं महाराज गगनादिव भास्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the kings saw a great radiance rise from the body of the king of Chedi, like the sun rising from the sky, great king."}},{"n":23,"text":"ततः कमलपत्राक्षं कृष्णं लोकनमस्कृतम् ।\nववन्दे तत्तदा तेजो विवेश च नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then that radiance saluted lotus-eyed Krishna, revered by the world, and entered him, lord of men."}},{"n":24,"text":"तदद्भुतममन्यन्त दृष्ट्वा सर्वे महीक्षितः ।\nयद्विवेश महाबाहुं तत्तेजः पुरुषोत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the kings thought it wondrous when that radiance entered the mighty-armed Purushottama."}},{"n":25,"text":"अनभ्रे प्रववर्ष द्यौः पपात ज्वलिताशनिः ।\nकृष्णेन निहते चैद्ये चचाल च वसुंधरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sky rained without a cloud, a blazing thunderbolt fell, and the earth shook when the Chedi king was slain by Krishna."}},{"n":26,"text":"ततः केचिन्महीपाला नाब्रुवंस्तत्र किंचन ।\nअतीतवाक्पथे काले प्रेक्षमाणा जनार्दनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then some of the kings said nothing there, only gazing at Janardana, since it was a time beyond words."}},{"n":27,"text":"हस्तैर्हस्ताग्रमपरे प्रत्यपीषन्नमर्षिताः ।\nअपरे दशनैरोष्ठानदशन्क्रोधमूर्छिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Others, enraged, pressed their fingertips together with their hands; others, overcome by anger, bit their lips with their teeth."}},{"n":28,"text":"रहस्तु केचिद्वार्ष्णेयं प्रशशंसुर्नराधिपाः ।\nकेचिदेव तु संरब्धा मध्यस्थास्त्वपरेऽभवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some kings praised the Vrishni in private; some remained furious, and others stayed neutral."}},{"n":29,"text":"प्रहृष्टाः केशवं जग्मुः संस्तुवन्तो महर्षयः ।\nब्राह्मणाश्च महात्मानः पार्थिवाश्च महाबलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great sages, great-souled brahmins and mighty kings went joyfully to Keshava, praising him."}},{"n":30,"text":"पाण्डवस्त्वब्रवीद्भ्रातॄन्सत्कारेण महीपतिम् ।\nदमघोषात्मजं वीरं संसाधयत मा चिरम् ।\nतथा च कृतवन्तस्ते भ्रातुर्वै शासनं तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandava said to his brothers: Give the king, hero son of Damaghosha, his last honours quickly. They did what their brother ordered then."}},{"n":31,"text":"चेदीनामाधिपत्ये च पुत्रमस्य महीपतिम् ।\nअभ्यषिञ्चत्तदा पार्थः सह तैर्वसुधाधिपैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Partha, with those kings, consecrated the dead king's son as ruler over the Chedis."}},{"n":32,"text":"ततः स कुरुराजस्य क्रतुः सर्वसमृद्धिमान् ।\nयूनां प्रीतिकरो राजन्संबभौ विपुलौजसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then that sacrifice of the Kuru king, richly complete, and giving joy to the young, shone, O king, with vast splendour."}},{"n":33,"text":"शान्तविघ्नः सुखारम्भः प्रभूतधनधान्यवान् ।\nअन्नवान्बहुभक्ष्यश्च केशवेन सुरक्षितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Its obstacles quieted, its beginning easy, rich in great wealth and grain, with abundant food and many dishes, it was well protected by Keshava."}},{"n":34,"text":"समापयामास च तं राजसूयं महाक्रतुम् ।\nतं तु यज्ञं महाबाहुरा समाप्तेर्जनार्दनः ।\nररक्ष भगवाञ्शौरिः शार्ङ्गचक्रगदाधरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And he completed that Rajasuya, the great sacrifice. The blessed Shauri, mighty-armed Janardana, bearer of the Sharnga bow, discus and mace, guarded that sacrifice until its end."}},{"n":35,"text":"ततस्त्ववभृथस्नातं धर्मराजं युधिष्ठिरम् ।\nसमस्तं पार्थिवं क्षत्रमभिगम्येदमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, when Yudhishthira, king of dharma, had bathed in the final ablution, all the royal Kshatriyas came to him and said:"}},{"n":36,"text":"दिष्ट्या वर्धसि धर्मज्ञ साम्राज्यं प्राप्तवान्विभो ।\nआजमीढाजमीढानां यशः संवर्धितं त्वया ।\nकर्मणैतेन राजेन्द्र धर्मश्च सुमहान्कृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The kings said: By good fortune you prosper, knower of dharma; lord, you have attained the imperial rank. Descendant of Ajamidha, you have increased the fame of the Ajamidha line, and by this deed, king of kings, you have won great dharma."}},{"n":37,"text":"आपृच्छामो नरव्याघ्र सर्वकामैः सुपूजिताः ।\nस्वराष्ट्राणि गमिष्यामस्तदनुज्ञातुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tiger among men, we take leave, honoured with all we desired. We shall go to our own realms; please give us leave."}},{"n":38,"text":"श्रुत्वा तु वचनं राज्ञां धर्मराजो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nयथार्हं पूज्य नृपतीन्भ्रातॄन्सर्वानुवाच ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the kings' words, Yudhishthira, king of dharma, honoured the kings as each deserved and said to all his brothers:"}},{"n":39,"text":"राजानः सर्व एवैते प्रीत्यास्मान्समुपागताः ।\nप्रस्थिताः स्वानि राष्ट्राणि मामापृच्छ्य परंतपाः ।\nतेऽनुव्रजत भद्रं वो विषयान्तं नृपोत्तमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said: All these kings, scourges of foes, came to us out of affection and now depart for their realms, taking leave of me. Go with them, best of kings, as far as the border of the land. May you be well."}},{"n":40,"text":"भ्रातुर्वचनमाज्ञाय पाण्डवा धर्मचारिणः ।\nयथार्हं नृपमुख्यांस्तानेकैकं समनुव्रजन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing their brother's order, the Pandavas, who followed dharma, accompanied each of those chief kings as was fitting."}},{"n":41,"text":"विराटमन्वयात्तूर्णं धृष्टद्युम्नः प्रतापवान् ।\nधनंजयो यज्ञसेनं महात्मानं महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mighty Dhrishtadyumna quickly followed Virata, and the great chariot-warrior Arjuna followed the great-souled Yajnasena."}},{"n":42,"text":"भीष्मं च धृतराष्ट्रं च भीमसेनो महाबलः ।\nद्रोणं च ससुतं वीरं सहदेवो महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mighty Bhimasena followed Bhishma and Dhritarashtra, and the great chariot-warrior Sahadeva followed the hero Drona and his son."}},{"n":43,"text":"नकुलः सुबलं राजन्सहपुत्रं समन्वयात् ।\nद्रौपदेयाः ससौभद्राः पार्वतीयान्महीपतीन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nakula, O king, followed Subala with his son, and the sons of Draupadi with the son of Subhadra followed the mountain kings."}},{"n":44,"text":"अन्वगच्छंस्तथैवान्यान्क्षत्रियान्क्षत्रियर्षभाः ।\nएवं संपूजितास्ते वै जग्मुर्विप्राश्च सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise bulls among Kshatriyas followed the other Kshatriyas. So honoured, the kings and the brahmins all departed."}},{"n":45,"text":"गतेषु पार्थिवेन्द्रेषु सर्वेषु भरतर्षभ ।\nयुधिष्ठिरमुवाचेदं वासुदेवः प्रतापवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When all the best of kings had gone, bull of the Bharatas, mighty Vasudeva said to Yudhishthira:"}},{"n":46,"text":"आपृच्छे त्वां गमिष्यामि द्वारकां कुरुनन्दन ।\nराजसूयं क्रतुश्रेष्ठं दिष्ट्या त्वं प्राप्तवानसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna said: I take leave of you, joy of the Kurus; I shall go to Dvaraka. By good fortune you have obtained the Rajasuya, best of sacrifices."}},{"n":47,"text":"तमुवाचैवमुक्तस्तु धर्मराण्मधुसूदनम् ।\nतव प्रसादाद्गोविन्द प्राप्तवानस्मि वै क्रतुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So addressed, Yudhishthira, king of dharma, said to Madhusudana: By your grace, Govinda, I have obtained the sacrifice."}},{"n":48,"text":"समस्तं पार्थिवं क्षत्रं त्वत्प्रसादाद्वशानुगम् ।\nउपादाय बलिं मुख्यं मामेव समुपस्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By your grace all the royal Kshatriyas have come under my sway and brought me their best tribute."}},{"n":49,"text":"न वयं त्वामृते वीर रंस्यामेह कथंचन ।\nअवश्यं चापि गन्तव्या त्वया द्वारवती पुरी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hero, we shall not be happy here in any way without you; yet you must surely go to the city of Dvaravati."}},{"n":50,"text":"एवमुक्तः स धर्मात्मा युधिष्ठिरसहायवान् ।\nअभिगम्याब्रवीत्प्रीतः पृथां पृथुयशा हरिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed, righteous, widely famed Hari, with Yudhishthira's company, went to Pritha and said happily:"}},{"n":51,"text":"साम्राज्यं समनुप्राप्ताः पुत्रास्तेऽद्य पितृष्वसः ।\nसिद्धार्था वसुमन्तश्च सा त्वं प्रीतिमवाप्नुहि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna said: Aunt, your sons have attained the imperial rank, their aims accomplished and rich in wealth; be glad."}},{"n":52,"text":"अनुज्ञातस्त्वया चाहं द्वारकां गन्तुमुत्सहे ।\nसुभद्रां द्रौपदीं चैव सभाजयत केशवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With your leave I wish to go to Dvaraka. Let Keshava be honoured by Subhadra and Draupadi."}},{"n":53,"text":"निष्क्रम्यान्तःपुराच्चैव युधिष्ठिरसहायवान् ।\nस्नातश्च कृतजप्यश्च ब्राह्मणान्स्वस्ति वाच्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having come out of the women's quarters with Yudhishthira in company, bathed, with his prayers said and the brahmins asked to pronounce blessings,"}},{"n":54,"text":"ततो मेघवरप्रख्यं स्यन्दनं वै सुकल्पितम् ।\nयोजयित्वा महाराज दारुकः प्रत्युपस्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Daruka, great king, then came up with the chariot, finely equipped and like a great cloud, yoked and ready."}},{"n":55,"text":"उपस्थितं रथं दृष्ट्वा तार्क्ष्यप्रवरकेतनम् ।\nप्रदक्षिणमुपावृत्य समारुह्य महामनाः ।\nप्रययौ पुण्डरीकाक्षस्ततो द्वारवतीं पुरीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the chariot with its banner of Garuda standing ready, the great-minded one circled it with his right side and climbed up. Then the lotus-eyed one set out for the city of Dvaravati."}},{"n":56,"text":"तं पद्भ्यामनुवव्राज धर्मराजो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nभ्रातृभिः सहितः श्रीमान्वासुदेवं महाबलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, king of dharma, glorious, with his brothers, followed mighty Vasudeva on foot."}},{"n":57,"text":"ततो मुहूर्तं संगृह्य स्यन्दनप्रवरं हरिः ।\nअब्रवीत्पुण्डरीकाक्षः कुन्तीपुत्रं युधिष्ठिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Hari, lotus-eyed, held his excellent chariot still for a moment and said to Yudhishthira, son of Kunti:"}},{"n":58,"text":"अप्रमत्तः स्थितो नित्यं प्रजाः पाहि विशां पते ।\nपर्जन्यमिव भूतानि महाद्रुममिवाण्डजाः ।\nबान्धवास्त्वोपजीवन्तु सहस्राक्षमिवामराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna said: Always be vigilant and protect your people, lord of men, as the rain-god protects beings, as a great tree protects birds, and let your kinsmen live by you as the immortals do by Indra of a thousand eyes."}},{"n":59,"text":"कृत्वा परस्परेणैवं संविदं कृष्णपाण्डवौ ।\nअन्योन्यं समनुज्ञाप्य जग्मतुः स्वगृहान्प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having thus come to an understanding, Krishna and the Pandava took leave of each other and each went to his own home."}},{"n":60,"text":"गते द्वारवतीं कृष्णे सात्वतप्रवरे नृप ।\nएको दुर्योधनो राजा शकुनिश्चापि सौबलः ।\nतस्यां सभायां दिव्यायामूषतुस्तौ नरर्षभौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Krishna, best of the Satvatas, had gone to Dvaravati, King Duryodhana and Shakuni, Subala's son, those two bulls among men, alone remained in that divine hall."}}]}]}